  "title": "TCP: Add check for out of order based on interpreted next sequence values",
  "description": "Fixes https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/15993\n\nThis adds a new edge case for identifying a packet as `Out-Of-Order`. If the current packet sequence matches what the next sequence _should have been_, but the current packet isn't the current latest value, then it should be marked as OOO.\n\nRecreation of https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/7737 with new branch name",
