        {
          "id": 1060418443,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@eugene.adell Yeah that's an issue, I'll look into now.\n\nSo should these two packets both be marked as OOO?\n\n![Screen_Shot_2022-08-12_at_7.12.08_PM](/uploads/f9d30e44d37eb97a947ff2e5b691e642/Screen_Shot_2022-08-12_at_7.12.08_PM.png)\n\nPacket 40 is an ACK that is using the sequence number from 41, and both should be valid - 40 counted as an ACK of packet 22, and 41 being the continuation of the New Session Ticket from 39. \n\nOr should only 41 be considered OOO?",
          "author": {
            "id": 2616346,
            "username": "jonluca",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "JonLuca De Caro",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
