        {
          "id": 1063053320,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Packet 40 hits this code path\n\n```\n    /* LOST PACKET\n     * If this segment is beyond the last seen nextseq we must\n     * have missed some previous segment\n     *\n     * We only check for this if we have actually seen segments prior to this\n     * one.\n     * RST packets are not checked for this.\n     */\n    if( tcpd->fwd->tcp_analyze_seq_info->nextseq\n    &&  GT_SEQ(seq, tcpd->fwd->tcp_analyze_seq_info->nextseq)\n    &&  (flags&(TH_RST))==0 ) {\n        if(!tcpd->ta) {\n            tcp_analyze_get_acked_struct(pinfo->num, seq, ack, TRUE, tcpd);\n        }\n        tcpd->ta->flags|=TCP_A_LOST_PACKET;\n\n        /* Disable BiF until an ACK is seen in the other direction */\n        tcpd->fwd->valid_bif = 0;\n    }\n```\n\nwhen in reality it probably shouldn't, right? It is simply an ACK using a sequence number that is OOO.\n\nShould both 40 and 41 be marked as OOO, or should 40 still be a \"TCP Previous segment not captured\" and only 41 is.\n\nAnd what should happen when `tcp_reassemble_out_of_order` is true?",
          "author": {
            "id": 2616346,
            "username": "jonluca",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "JonLuca De Caro",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/2616346/avatar.png?v=1789018034",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jonluca"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-14T17:25:33.575Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-11T07:59:43.108Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 171150726,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6797213/avatar.png?v=1789284959",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/eugene.adell"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2024-10-11T07:59:43.108Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7738,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1068416047,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Should both 40 and 41 be marked as OOO, or should 40 still be a \"TCP Previous segment not captured\" and only 41 is.\nThe latter is correct (40 : not captured comment, 41 : OOO)\n\nNot all protocols want OOO reassembly, hence this boolean.\n\nI posted last year a simplistic MR for similar cases but had to revert because of side effects. I'll maybe re-open this work, but it's necessary to know we also have the opposite problem (packets erroneously interpreted as OOO).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6797213/avatar.png?v=1789284959",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/eugene.adell"
          },
